ODW9503 [*] `message_post` overrides a method decorated with `@api.returns`, which `_inherit` does not carry over — only Python bases do. Without it the override returns a recordset over RPC instead of an id. Add `@api.returns("mail.message", lambda value: value.id)`.
  --> api_returns.py:12:9
   |
10 |     _inherit = "project.task"
11 |
12 |     def message_post(self, **kwargs):  # ODW9503
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^
13 |         return super().message_post(**kwargs)
   |
help: Add `@api.returns("mail.message", lambda value: value.id)`
   |
11 |
12 +     @api.returns("mail.message", lambda value: value.id)
13 |     def message_post(self, **kwargs):  # ODW9503
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

ODW9503 [*] `find_or_create` overrides a method decorated with `@api.returns`, which `_inherit` does not carry over — only Python bases do. Without it the override returns a recordset over RPC instead of an id. Add `@api.returns("self", lambda value: value.id)`.
  --> api_returns.py:26:9
   |
24 |     _inherit = "res.partner"
25 |
26 |     def find_or_create(self, emails, **kwargs):  # ODW9503
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
27 |         return super().find_or_create(emails, **kwargs)
   |
help: Add `@api.returns("self", lambda value: value.id)`
   |
25 |
26 +     @api.returns("self", lambda value: value.id)
27 |     def find_or_create(self, emails, **kwargs):  # ODW9503
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

ODW9503 [*] `main_partner` overrides a method decorated with `@api.returns`, which `_inherit` does not carry over — only Python bases do. Without it the override returns a recordset over RPC instead of an id. Add `@api.returns("self")`.
  --> api_returns.py:29:9
   |
27 |         return super().find_or_create(emails, **kwargs)
28 |
29 |     def main_partner(self):  # ODW9503 (16.0-17.0 only)
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^
30 |         return super().main_partner()
   |
help: Add `@api.returns("self")`
   |
28 |
29 +     @api.returns("self")
30 |     def main_partner(self):  # ODW9503 (16.0-17.0 only)
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

ODW9503 [*] `create_or_replace` overrides a method decorated with `@api.returns`, which `_inherit` does not carry over — only Python bases do. Without it the override returns a recordset over RPC instead of an id. Add `@api.returns("self", lambda value: value.id)`.
  --> api_returns.py:44:9
   |
42 |     _inherit = "ir.filters"
43 |
44 |     def create_or_replace(self, vals):  # ODW9503
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
45 |         return super().create_or_replace(vals)
   |
help: Add `@api.returns("self", lambda value: value.id)`
   |
43 |
44 +     @api.returns("self", lambda value: value.id)
45 |     def create_or_replace(self, vals):  # ODW9503
   |
